      diveDeep: 'The H-R diagram is a key tool in stellar astronomy. The main sequence is a diagonal band from upper-left (hot, bright, massive blue stars) to lower-right (cool, dim, small red dwarf stars) where stars spend most of their lives fusing hydrogen. Giants and supergiants are in the upper-right (high luminosity, cool temperatures). White dwarfs are in the lower-left (hot but dim — small remnants of dead stars). Our Sun is a G-type main sequence star. Students should know the life cycle: main sequence → red giant (for sun-like stars) → planetary nebula → white dwarf; or for massive stars → supergiant → supernova → neutron star or black hole.',
