      diveDeep: 'Eclipse conditions require precise alignment of the Sun, Earth, and Moon (syzygy). Lunar eclipse: Sun → Earth → Moon alignment; Earth\'s shadow falls on the Moon; visible from anywhere on the night side of Earth. Solar eclipse: Sun → Moon → Earth alignment; Moon\'s shadow falls on Earth; visible only along a narrow path. Eclipses don\'t occur every month because the Moon\'s orbit is tilted ~5° relative to Earth\'s orbital plane. Students should know that a lunar eclipse always occurs at full moon and a solar eclipse always at new moon — but not every full/new moon produces an eclipse due to the orbital tilt.',
