      explanation: 'The principle of original horizontality states that sediments are deposited in horizontal layers. If layers are found tilted or folded, it indicates that forces have deformed them after deposition.',
      diveDeep: 'The four key principles of relative dating that students must know: (1) Original Horizontality — sedimentary layers are deposited horizontally; tilted layers were deformed. (2) Superposition — in undisturbed strata, older layers are on the bottom. (3) Cross-cutting Relationships — any feature that cuts across rock layers is younger than the layers it cuts. (4) Inclusion — fragments included in a rock are older than the rock containing them. Uniformitarianism (James Hutton) states that the same geologic processes operating today operated in the past at the same rates — "the present is the key to the past." All five principles are tested on the Regents.',
