      diveDeep: 'Climate types are primarily determined by temperature and precipitation patterns. Key climates to know: Tropical rainforest (hot year-round, high precipitation every month); Desert (very low precipitation, extreme temperature swings); Mediterranean (hot dry summers, mild wet winters); Humid continental (large temperature range, year-round precipitation — typical of northeastern US, northern Europe); Tundra (very cold, very low precipitation, short cool summers); Ice cap (always below freezing). The humid continental climate is characteristic of much of New York State. Students should be able to read a climograph and identify the climate type from its temperature and precipitation patterns.',
