      diveDeep: 'Cold front characteristics: steep frontal boundary (nearly vertical); fast-moving; causes warm moist air to be rapidly lifted → brief, intense precipitation (thunderstorms, heavy rain, possible hail); after passage → cold air moves in, skies clear, temperatures drop sharply, winds shift counterclockwise (veer from SW to NW). Warm front characteristics: gentle slope; slow-moving; gradual lifting of cold air → widespread, steady precipitation over a large area; after passage → warmer temperatures, higher humidity. Students should know the weather sequence associated with a typical mid-latitude cyclone: warm front approaches (clouds thicken, precipitation begins), warm sector (mild, humid), cold front (intense precipitation), cold front passes (clearing, cooler).',
